#message 28 "URI QUEST INSTRUCTION MANUAL\n\nSECTION 1. INTRODUCTION\n\nSeasoned Sierra Adventure game players may skip this section.\n\nAGI Games are adventure games in which your character moves around the screen (according to where you move it), and all actions are performed through a typing interface. You type in what you want your character to do, and you will get a response."
#message 29 "Let's say you see a tree on the screen. You might want to look at the tree. Try typing \"look at the tree\" and press ENTER. The response may be a description of the tree, or maybe you'll get a clue that you have to do something further with the tree."
#message 30 "URI Quest understands many verbs and nouns. In most cases, you can omit words like \"a\", \"at\", \"the\", etc... The interpreter will ignore these words. In other words, just typing something like \"look chair\", \"use guitar\" or \"get coin\" are enough. Other times, you might want to be more specific, as in \"look behind bureau\" or \"look under bed\". Either way, this is the basic method for playing this game."
#message 31 "You can move your character with the arrow keys or with the numeric keypad. Using the numeric keypad allows your character to move diagonally in addition to the four basic directions of the arrow keys.\n\nIf you press the ESC key, the top of the screen will turn into a menu bar. You have a number choices to choose from up there. The choices are as follows:"
#message 32 "ABOUT URI QUEST: Try it and see what happens.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS: You're reading them.\n\nSAVE GAME: You can save your game's progress at just about any point. Choose this option and follow the instructions.\n\nRESTORE GAME: You can load any game that you've previously saved.\n\nRESTART GAME: Restart the game from the beginning."
#message 33 "INVENTORY: Lists the items that you've picked up.\n\nSEE OBJECT: Allows you to choose an item that you've picked up and look at it. A description of the item is also provided.\n\nCLOCK ON/OFF: Turns the in-game timer on or off.\n\nPAUSE GAME: Pauses the game in progress.\n\nChoosing an option or pressing the ESC key again will exit from this menu."
#message 34 "SECTION 2.\nGAMEPLAY TIPS AND HINTS\n\nCareful examination of every room is the only way you will succeed. LOOK at everything you see. Type LOOK or LOOK AROUND in every room to get a general description of your surroundings. The response may give you some hints about what you should do next. In some cases, it may not. If you see something on your screen that you want to check out, don't be afraid to try it, even though the game did not give you a hint that you should."
#message 35 "To complete your quest, you will have to acquire many items along the way. Try to GET anything you think might be useful. It's always a good idea to LOOK (by pressing F4) at every object you pick up. There may be more to it than meets the eye."
#message 36 "Don't be afraid to try typing anything you can think of to solve a particular puzzle. If you think you know what to do, but the game doesn't understand it, try rephrasing your request. Every effort has been made to think of every possible request the player can type, but I'm sure I haven't thought of everything. Try saying things different ways, usually the simpler the better."
#message 37 "This should be enough to get you going. You'll soon get the hang of it. Good luck!\n\nComments, questions, & suggestions can be sent to me, Jeff Carroll."
#message 38 "To contact me, get updates, hints or any other general info about URI QUEST, go to the URI QUEST Homepage:\n\nhttp://www.jeffcarroll.net/uriquest/"
